# The fetch / decode / dispatch tails shared by most instructions, and the
# effective address helpers for the indexed addressing modes.

@00000 cb
    ===========================================================================
    Indexed addressing mode decode table (256 entries of two instructions)
    ===========================================================================
    Indexed by the high byte of a 68020 extension word (D/A, register, W/L,
    scale).  Each entry puts the index register, sign-extended and/or scaled
    as that byte requests, into rtn_addr and branches to the routine that
    finishes the calculation: one of the ea_add_index entries for a brief
    extension word, or one of the ea_full_format entries when bit 8 of the
    extension word is set.

    On entry: addr = base register + sign-extended d8, base_disp = d8 (and
    still holds the whole extension word in its low byte for the full-format
    test), LR = return address.

    This table is at the very start of the code block so that
    code_ptr + (extension word high byte * 8) addresses an entry directly.

@05F10 ea_indexed_dispatch
    Dispatch on the high byte of the extension word in prefetch_data into
    the table at cb, with CTR holding the operation routine to continue at.
05F14 rtn_addr = extension word high byte * 8
05F24 call the table entry; it returns here with addr complete

@05F40 ea_add_index_x2
@05F44 ea_add_index
    Brief extension word: addr += index and return.
@05F4C ea_add_index_x4
@05F58 ea_add_index_x8

@05F80 ea_full_format_x2
@05F84 ea_full_format
    Full-format (68020) extension word.  The low byte of the extension word
    is copied into CR6/CR7 and tested bit by bit:
    .
        cr6.lt  BS   base register suppress
        cr6.gt  IS   index suppress
        cr6.eq/so    BD size (01 null, 10 word, 11 long)
        cr7.gt/eq/so I/IS memory indirection selector
    .
    The d8 that the caller optimistically added is first backed out.
05F8C undo the d8 added by the caller
@05FE0 ea_full_format_x8
@05FE4 ea_full_format_x4
@06064 ea_reserved_format
    Reserved full-format encoding: return a recognisably bogus address.

@06080 fetch_skip_word
    Step over one extension word, then fetch.
@06084 fetch
    Decode and dispatch the next 68K instruction.  This is the plain ending
    of an emulation routine; most routines carry their own copy of these
    four instructions interleaved with their last few operations.
@06088 fetch_decoded
    As fetch, when DECODE1 has already been done.
@060A0 fetch_skip_long
    Step over a 32-bit extension, then fetch.

@060C0 update_vc_zero
    Clear V and C (N and Z were set by the caller), then fetch.
@060E0 update_nzvcx_zero
    Result was zero and nothing was borrowed: N=0, Z=1, V=C=X=0, then fetch.
@06100 update_nzvc_zero
    N=0, Z=1, V=0, C=0, then fetch.  (The name is the one used for this
    routine in US5790825, figure 9.)
@06120 update_nzvc_zero_skip_word
    As update_nzvc_zero, after stepping over one extension word.

@06140 test_byte
    Set N and Z from the byte in data, clear V and C, then fetch.
@06144 test_data
    Set N and Z from data (already left-justified), clear V and C, fetch.
@06160 test_byte_skip_word
@06164 test_data_skip_word
